# R7-1 — pin the working tree to LF.
#
# This machine (and most Windows clones) has core.autocrlf=true. Without this
# file the fixture store checks out with CRLF, which makes
# tests/fixtures/api/make-store.mjs's write-if-different check fail on EVERY
# call: all 9 files get rewritten through `${abs}.${pid}.tmp` + rename by every
# test-file process at once, exposing .tmp files to the file-census walks in
# tests/audit-pathb.test.mjs and tests/fixes-audit.test.mjs. Today
# `git ls-files --eol` reports the store as i/lf w/lf and makeStore() is a
# no-op — this file is what keeps that true on someone else's clone.
#
# The reader depends on LF too: server/jsonl.mjs splits on \n only, and the
# byte offsets and `bytes` figures the tests assert are LF offsets.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The transcript fixtures are BYTE-EXACT inputs — sizes, byteOffsets and line
# censuses are asserted against them. No EOL conversion may ever touch them,
# whatever a future core.eol says. (Diffs here render as binary; these files
# are generated by make-store.mjs / extract-fixtures.mjs, not hand-edited.)
tests/fixtures/api/store/** -text
tests/fixtures/reader/** -text
tests/fixtures/*.jsonl -text
